1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,916
For fifty-four years, Real Madrid came to
Greece and could not win.

2
00:00:06,246 --> 00:00:10,939
Nine games. Six draws. Three defeats.

3
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:13,785
In Spain they had a word for it.

4
00:00:14,115 --> 00:00:16,947
Maleficio. A curse.

5
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:20,687
This is the story of every one of those
nights.

6
00:00:21,017 --> 00:00:26,244
A European final in Piraeus. Three Athens
clubs.

7
00:00:26,574 --> 00:00:29,797
Olympiacos, Panathinaikos, AEK.

8
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:34,776
From Madrid to Athens is a long way across
the Mediterranean.

9
00:00:35,106 --> 00:00:40,050
Real Madrid have made the trip for finals,
for group games, for nights they

10
00:00:40,090 --> 00:00:41,426
would rather forget.

11
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:47,851
And tonight, the fourth of November 2026,
Real Madrid are back.

12
00:00:48,181 --> 00:00:50,818
At the new home of AEK.

13
00:00:52,310 --> 00:00:56,623
It started with a final. Not even against
a Greek club.

14
00:00:57,020 --> 00:01:02,612
May 1971. The Cup Winners' Cup final, the
first

15
00:01:02,652 --> 00:01:05,345
European final ever played in Greece.

16
00:01:05,675 --> 00:01:10,685
Real Madrid against Chelsea, at the
Karaiskakis in Piraeus.

17
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:16,530
On the way they had beaten Hibernians of
Malta, Wacker Innsbruck,

18
00:01:16,770 --> 00:01:18,551
Cardiff City and PSV Eindhoven.

19
00:01:18,940 --> 00:01:23,375
Miguel Muñoz's Madrid still had Gento and
Amancio.

20
00:01:23,705 --> 00:01:25,946
Forty-two thousand watched.

21
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:30,520
Peter Osgood scored for Chelsea after
fifty-six minutes.

22
00:01:30,850 --> 00:01:33,694
Madrid were going home with nothing.

23
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:36,365
Then, in the last minute, Zoco.

24
00:01:36,405 --> 00:01:39,200
One–one. Extra time, no winner.

25
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:42,447
There were no penalties in those days.

26
00:01:42,777 --> 00:01:47,614
The final was played again, forty-eight
hours later, on the same pitch.

27
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:52,535
Dempsey and Osgood put Chelsea two up
before half-time.

28
00:01:53,005 --> 00:01:57,426
Fleitas pulled one back. It was not
enough.

29
00:01:57,820 --> 00:02:00,816
Real Madrid's first two games in Greece.

30
00:02:00,966 --> 00:02:05,245
A draw and a defeat. The curse had its
first page.

31
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:10,366
Quick one, before we go on. If you've ever
stood in the rain for ninety minutes

32
00:02:10,406 --> 00:02:13,297
and called it a good day, you belong here.

33
00:02:13,447 --> 00:02:18,483
Subscribe to FanLife Football Stories, and
take your place on the terrace.

34
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:25,090
Fourteen years later, Madrid came back to
Athens to play a Greek club for the

35
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:25,809
first time.

36
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:32,125
September 1985. The UEFA Cup, first round.

37
00:02:32,455 --> 00:02:35,783
AEK Athens, at the Olympic Stadium.

38
00:02:36,113 --> 00:02:40,424
39,819 inside.

39
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:45,850
Pavlos Papaioannou scored the only goal,
with Márton Esterházy standing right in

40
00:02:45,890 --> 00:02:47,986
front of the Madrid goalkeeper.

41
00:02:48,026 --> 00:02:50,078
AEK one, Real Madrid nil.

42
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:54,199
Jacek Gmoch's AEK had given Real Madrid
their first defeat at the hands of a

43
00:02:54,239 --> 00:02:57,495
Greek club, in Greece.

44
00:02:57,900 --> 00:03:03,266
Madrid won the second leg five–nil, and
went on to win the whole competition.

45
00:03:03,416 --> 00:03:05,672
But in Athens, they had lost.

46
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:12,262
In the nineties, Olympiacos played their
big European nights at the Olympic

47
00:03:12,302 --> 00:03:15,217
Stadium. Real Madrid came twice.

48
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:21,462
November 1997. Nil–nil. That season Madrid

49
00:03:21,502 --> 00:03:23,939
won their seventh European Cup.

50
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:30,427
September 1999. 70,800 people,

51
00:03:30,677 --> 00:03:34,001
and a goalkeeper of eighteen in the Madrid
goal.

52
00:03:34,331 --> 00:03:38,803
Iker Casillas, eighteen years and a
hundred and eighteen days.

53
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:42,151
Giovanni scored after eleven minutes.

54
00:03:42,481 --> 00:03:47,072
Sávio and Roberto Carlos turned it around
before half-time.

55
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:51,413
Then Giovanni again. Then Zahović.

56
00:03:51,743 --> 00:03:54,120
Three–two Olympiacos.

57
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:56,673
And in the eightieth minute, Raúl.

58
00:03:56,713 --> 00:03:57,812
Three–three.

59
00:03:58,180 --> 00:04:00,939
The Irish Times called him the saviour.

60
00:04:01,089 --> 00:04:04,606
Madrid won the Champions League again that
season.

61
00:04:04,756 --> 00:04:06,172
Not in Athens.

62
00:04:07,710 --> 00:04:12,346
In 2002, two Athens clubs, seven months
apart.

63
00:04:12,740 --> 00:04:17,910
March. Panathinaikos at Leoforos, their
old ground on

64
00:04:17,950 --> 00:04:23,614
Alexandras Avenue. Madrid had already won
the group, and Del Bosque sent a

65
00:04:23,654 --> 00:04:24,496
young team.

66
00:04:24,860 --> 00:04:27,642
Liberopoulos after nine minutes.

67
00:04:27,972 --> 00:04:33,879
Morientes two minutes later. Then Goumas,
and Panathinaikos led again.

68
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:38,621
In the eightieth minute, a substitute in
his first Champions League match.

69
00:04:38,661 --> 00:04:41,278
Javier Portillo. Two–two.

70
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:47,233
October. AEK, at the old Nikos Goumas in
Nea Filadelfeia.

71
00:04:47,563 --> 00:04:52,004
Madrid brought Figo, Zidane, Raúl and
Roberto Carlos.

72
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:55,385
After six minutes, Tsartas from a free
kick.

73
00:04:55,535 --> 00:05:00,940
Zidane equalised. Then Maladenis and
Nikolaidis, two headers in three

74
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:04,273
minutes. AEK three, Madrid one.

75
00:05:04,660 --> 00:05:08,624
Zidane again before half-time. Guti on the
hour.

76
00:05:08,664 --> 00:05:09,763
Three–three.

77
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:13,622
The ground was not even full; tickets were
expensive.

78
00:05:13,772 --> 00:05:19,381
The ones who came saw what Athens Voice
later called perhaps the best match ever

79
00:05:19,421 --> 00:05:24,004
played in Greece. When Zidane came off,
the whole ground applauded him.

80
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:30,204
Dušan Bajević had coached Olympiacos
against Madrid

81
00:05:30,244 --> 00:05:33,858
in 1999. Now he was on the AEK bench.

82
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:37,598
Vicente del Bosque did not blame his
defence.

83
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:41,689
AEK drew all six of their group games that
season.

84
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:45,299
And in Spain, the morning papers wrote the
word again.

85
00:05:45,449 --> 00:05:46,752
Maleficio.

86
00:05:48,270 --> 00:05:54,107
In 2004 the Karaiskakis was rebuilt, and
Olympiacos came

87
00:05:54,147 --> 00:05:55,455
home to Piraeus.

88
00:05:55,860 --> 00:06:01,520
December 2005. Madrid had a new coach,
Juan Ramón

89
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:04,160
López Caro, in his first match.

90
00:06:04,490 --> 00:06:08,570
Sergio Ramos headed them in front after
seven minutes.

91
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:14,481
Bulut equalised. And in the eighty-seventh
minute, an old enemy from

92
00:06:14,521 --> 00:06:17,091
Barcelona. Rivaldo.

93
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:20,916
Olympiacos two, Real Madrid one.

94
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:23,976
Sky Sports had the headline that night.

95
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:28,057
November 2007, and Madrid were back.

96
00:06:28,207 --> 00:06:34,095
33,500 inside. Van Nistelrooy hit the
woodwork, so

97
00:06:34,135 --> 00:06:36,170
did Raúl. Nil–nil.

98
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:42,295
And in the Olympiacos defence that night
stood Raúl Bravo, who had played for

99
00:06:42,335 --> 00:06:45,576
Real Madrid on the same pitch in 2005.

100
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:48,515
Then eighteen years without a visit.

101
00:06:50,030 --> 00:06:55,150
November 2025. Karaiskakis again.

102
00:06:55,300 --> 00:07:00,628
Xabi Alonso against José Luis Mendilibar,
the man who had won

103
00:07:00,668 --> 00:07:03,179
Olympiacos their European trophy.

104
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:06,049
After eight minutes, Chiquinho.

105
00:07:06,379 --> 00:07:10,986
One–nil Olympiacos. The curse was awake.

106
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:15,148
Then Kylian Mbappé. Twenty-two minutes.

107
00:07:15,298 --> 00:07:20,874
Twenty-four. Twenty-nine. A hat-trick in
six minutes and forty-two

108
00:07:20,914 --> 00:07:21,536
seconds.

109
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:26,947
Taremi pulled one back. Mbappé scored his
fourth on the hour.

110
00:07:27,277 --> 00:07:31,180
El Kaabi made it four–three in the
eighty-first minute.

111
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:36,892
Four–three. Real Madrid's first win at
Olympiacos, at the fifth attempt.

112
00:07:36,932 --> 00:07:38,900
Their first win in Greece.

113
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:41,771
Xabi Alonso said it plainly.

114
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:47,811
Ten games in Greece. One win, six draws,
three defeats.

115
00:07:48,910 --> 00:07:53,220
Tonight, at 19:45 Athens time, the
eleventh.

116
00:07:53,370 --> 00:07:56,370
Champions League, league phase, matchday
four.

117
00:07:56,780 --> 00:08:02,458
AEK's new ground stands where the Nikos
Goumas stood, the ground of the

118
00:08:02,498 --> 00:08:06,754
three–three. It opened in 2022.

119
00:08:07,084 --> 00:08:09,802
Real Madrid have never played there.

120
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:13,478
José Mourinho on the Madrid bench.

121
00:08:13,808 --> 00:08:19,129
Marko Nikolić for AEK, champions of Greece
for the fourteenth time.

122
00:08:19,459 --> 00:08:22,580
And up front for AEK, Luka Jović.

123
00:08:22,910 --> 00:08:25,606
A former Real Madrid striker.

124
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:29,208
Madrid have nine points from three games.

125
00:08:29,538 --> 00:08:34,648
AEK have three. On paper, there is no
contest.

126
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:38,104
But in Athens, paper has never meant much.

127
00:08:38,434 --> 00:08:43,854
Ask Papaioannou. Ask Tsartas. Ask Rivaldo.

128
00:08:44,260 --> 00:08:46,965
Fifty-four years of nights like these.

129
00:08:47,115 --> 00:08:50,454
Whoever you sing for tonight, you know why
they matter.

130
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:56,106
Every match in this film is waiting in the
FanLife archive, with the games, the

131
00:08:56,146 --> 00:08:58,709
trivia and the stories of the whole club.

132
00:08:58,859 --> 00:09:02,831
Come and play it at fanlife.dubelteam.com.

133
00:09:02,981 --> 00:09:07,867
And if this story was yours too,
subscribe, and the next one will find you.
